meta {
  name: Get Trip POD Settings
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/trips/{{tripId}}/v1/settings/epod
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  POD settings of the torg that owns the given trip, plus what they resolve to for that trip.
  Access is limited to VAHN_ADMIN, TORG_ADMIN/FLEET_OWNER/TRUCK_MANAGER of the owning torg, or the
  trip's actually-assigned driver (a DRIVER-role caller who isn't assigned to this specific trip
  is rejected with 403, not just anyone with the DRIVER role).

  Verified live on staging (2026-09-10) against trip 1325 (torg 315, POD settings saved but
  completion radius disabled), driver-authenticated:

  {
    "data": {
      "driverUploadEnabled": true,
      "completionRadiusEnabled": false,
      "completionRadiusMeters": null,
      "remainingDistance": 211.77
    },
    "message": "Success",
    "statusCode": 200,
    "success": true
  }

  As of PR #932 (open against develop, not yet merged/promoted to staging as of 2026-09-10), the
  response also gains `completionRadiusRemainingDistanceMeters` — see "Get Trip By ID" in this
  same folder for what it means and an illustrative value. It wasn't present in the response above
  because completionRadiusEnabled is false for this trip's torg, not because it's unmerged — but
  it genuinely is also unmerged, so re-verify once staging has PR #932.

  400 if the trip doesn't exist or has no owning torg; 403 if the caller isn't authorized for this
  trip specifically.
}
